Class-level: `@Schema(name="OwnerFields")`, `@JsonTypeName("OwnerFields")`, generated by OpenAPI SpringCodegen 7.23.0. Required-args constructor is `(firstName, lastName, city, telephone)`.

The response DTO is `OwnerDto` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerDto.java` (not read in full — the pipeline only maps into it via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`).

Important nuance: the OfficeFloor pipeline does NOT rely on the JSR-380 annotations above for its checks — required-field enforcement, telephone E.164, postcode range, email syntax, etc. are all done imperatively in the function steps and raise the custom escalations below. The annotation-driven `MethodArgumentNotValidException` path (see §4) is a separate/global validation layer.

